{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A vendor destination’s encoder writes each record as the vendor’s JSON. This module has the parts"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every such encoder needs, so each vendor module writes only its own format:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/PropertyJSON\/documentation\/PropertyJSON\/PropertyReader","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" reads an event’s properties through its schema in a "},{"code":"TrackingPlan","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"writes a "},{"code":"Sensitive","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" value only when asked to and the record reveals it."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"EventRecord.standardContext","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the standard context (app, device, locale, network, operating","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"system) as JSON, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"flattened(separator:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" turns nested JSON into one level of dotted keys.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Date.iso8601Timestamp"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Date.millisecondsSince1970()"},{"text":" are the two timestamp formats vendors","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"take, both rounded down to the millisecond.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"EventRecord.pseudonymousIdentity","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is the record’s session, or the record itself when it has"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"none, and "},{"code":"EventRecord.deduplicationID","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","t